 (--skew-x)) skewY(var(--skew-y))\; transform-origin: var(--origin-x) var(-
 -origin-y)\; } If watercolor has ever intimidated you\, this welcoming cla
 ss is designed just for you. Guided by Nancy Ballard\, you’ll ease into 
 the medium with simple\, approachable techniques that take the fear out of
  painting. Through relaxed exercises and encouraging instruction\, you’l
 l learn how watercolor really works—without pressure or perfection—whi
 le building confidence step by step. Emphasizing play\, curiosity\, and sm
 all wins\, this class creates a supportive space to explore color\, brushw
 ork\, and flow. Perfect for absolute beginners or anyone ready to let go o
 f fear and finally give watercolor a try. Materials Please bring: Your Wat
 ercolors Provided: Paper\, plus a mat\, backing\, and sleeve so your piece
  will be ready for framing This class is located in the PAC classroom.&nbs
 p\; About the Teacher:&nbsp\; Nancy Ballard 's love of art began in childh
 ood\, when she first discovered the magic of brush and paint—a sense of 
 wonder that continues to shape her work today. After a full life as a moth
 er\, grandmother\, and corporate professional\, she returned to art follow
 ing her retirement in 2006\, studying watercolor with Mary L. Harden at St
 rybing Arboretum. In 2009\, she was recognized as a Master Artist of Botan
 ical Illustration by the San Francisco Botanical Garden Society. Nancy has
  also worked as a gallery curator and exhibiting artist throughout the Bay
  Area\, sharing her botanical work in galleries\, wineries\, hospitals\, a
 nd nonprofit spaces while supporting environmental awareness through art. 
 Learn More:&nbsp\; www.nancyballard.com #block-2edb6de5c709af3375cb { --st
